      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The planned installation included an inverter that was borderline sufficient. I had thought that the consequence of its capacity being breached would be that the system works simply draw more from the grid rather than from the battery. The consequence on testing the system with 10kW inverter was that, when too much power was being drawn (eg. oven, AC and one other appliance), power was lost to the whole house. Clearly that wasn't acceptable, so Andrew from Clean Energy Solutions promptly attached to have the 10kW inverter replaced with the 15kW model. Now the system works as hoped. I only wish I'd requested/applied for an extra stackable unit or two of kWh to take advantage of the current incentive. Ah, well even with three incentive the cost for additional kWh is still not cheap. I expect I'll be looking to beef up the battery down the track. Meanwhile, I'm very happy with the quoting, subsequent installation and post installation service provided by Clean Energy Solutions Albury.",
